# ═══ META-LESSONS ═══
L1: `crate::runtime::HookRuntime` works (re-export from `pub use runtime::{HookRuntime}`), but `crate::runtime::IsolationMode` does NOT (since IsolationMode is in `hook_runtime.rs` not in `runtime/` directory). Two ways to fix: re-export in lib.rs OR use the right path `crate::hook_runtime::IsolationMode`. Path fix is simpler.
L2: `pub mod runtime;` in lib.rs is a DIRECTORY (src/runtime/), separate from `pub mod hook_runtime;` which is `src/hook_runtime.rs`. The re-export `pub use runtime::{HookRuntime}` brings the type from runtime/ to the root — but custom types in hook_runtime.rs are NOT auto-re-exported.
L3: `AccessPath` is an ENUM (Symbol/OutcomeKey/CrdtNode/Path variants), not a struct. Path-rewriting only applies to the `Path(String)` variant; other variants are passed through unchanged.
L4: SQLite WAL + Mutex<Connection> per-instance is the right concurrency model for low-rate write/read workloads (one event per tool outcome). Higher rates would need connection pooling.
L5: For the E0061 error on `rusqlite::Error::ToSqlConversionFailure` — it's a tuple variant with 1 arg (Box<dyn Error>), not 2. The 2-arg form includes a String but is only in older versions.
L6: `pub enum IsolationMode { Solo, Worktree(PathBuf) }` with `Default` impl — clean pattern for optional isolation that doesn't change the existing API surface.

